1
00:00:12,730 --> 00:00:15,550
♪I lean and gaze at misty waves afar♪

2
00:00:16,010 --> 00:00:18,320
♪Tears fall on the ancient road
'neath the setting sun♪

3
00:00:19,330 --> 00:00:21,460
♪One lone shadow on the cold river♪

4
00:00:21,460 --> 00:00:23,910
♪In dreams, I return to the old window♪

5
00:00:25,840 --> 00:00:28,670
♪Mountains stretch, the road home fades♪

6
00:00:29,320 --> 00:00:32,030
♪A flute cries out, hooves hurry on♪

7
00:00:32,460 --> 00:00:34,790
♪My heart adrift beneath a frosted moon♪

8
00:00:34,820 --> 00:00:38,220
♪Drinking alone, I mourn our parting♪

9
00:00:38,370 --> 00:00:40,050
♪Night turns cold, wind stirs the veil♪

10
00:00:40,060 --> 00:00:41,760
♪Old robes recall forgotten days♪

11
00:00:41,760 --> 00:00:43,570
♪Heart sore, a lone goose flies south♪

12
00:00:43,580 --> 00:00:45,230
♪Where shall I send this letter?♪

13
00:00:45,230 --> 00:00:47,760
♪Lost in thought through endless nights♪

14
00:00:47,770 --> 00:00:49,000
♪Love runs deep, dreams linger on♪

15
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:51,390
♪Only sorrow remains♪

16
00:00:51,640 --> 00:00:53,340
♪A cup of wine, my shadow makes us two♪

17
00:00:53,350 --> 00:00:54,980
♪Drunk and lost through flashing blades♪

18
00:00:54,990 --> 00:00:56,870
♪I curse how swiftly the years pass by♪

19
00:00:56,880 --> 00:00:58,580
♪The wandering road goes on♪

20
00:00:58,590 --> 00:01:01,020
♪Desolate, time frosts my youthful hair♪

21
00:01:01,030 --> 00:01:02,340
♪Through the years, love still burns♪

22
00:01:02,340 --> 00:01:04,530
♪A thousand tears fall♪

23
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:08,030
♪Worlds apart, tears stain my sleeves♪

24
00:01:08,150 --> 00:01:11,300
♪Old dreams haunt my heart,
tears cloud my eyes♪

25
00:01:11,460 --> 00:01:13,340
♪Heartbroken, soul-worn,
pain won't fade♪

26
00:01:13,340 --> 00:01:14,820
♪Moonlight westward, the night drags on♪

27
00:01:14,830 --> 00:01:17,920
♪The years have left their scars♪

28
00:01:18,080 --> 00:01:21,280
♪Autumn winds sweep leaves;
shadows pair♪

29
00:01:21,440 --> 00:01:24,590
♪The past fades like smoke;
tears fall♪

30
00:01:24,740 --> 00:01:26,820
♪My heart lies broken♪

31
00:01:26,830 --> 00:01:30,150
♪Lost in thought through endless nights♪

32
00:01:30,150 --> 00:01:34,980
[Love Legend]

33
00:01:35,100 --> 00:01:38,780
[Episode 6]

34
00:01:41,700 --> 00:01:42,970
- Mine looks better.
- This one's nice.

35
00:01:49,620 --> 00:01:50,310
- Sir.
- Sir.

36
00:02:07,480 --> 00:02:08,550
Allow me to explain.

37
00:02:09,080 --> 00:02:10,630
This is a soothing incense bead.

38
00:02:10,630 --> 00:02:12,560
Last night, I put it by my pillow

39
00:02:12,560 --> 00:02:13,850
and slept like a baby.

40
00:02:15,160 --> 00:02:16,960
Lu's is a calming bead.

41
00:02:17,090 --> 00:02:18,210
It clears the mind and qi.

42
00:02:18,980 --> 00:02:20,030
Ruoming's is...

43
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:28,430
Too flashy.

44
00:02:28,430 --> 00:02:29,190
Take them all off.

45
00:02:39,590 --> 00:02:40,770
Tonight, we go to the Blood Jade Mine.

46
00:02:41,260 --> 00:02:42,680
We must expose Chen Daohua.

47
00:02:43,060 --> 00:02:44,650
He killed people and blew up the mine.

48
00:02:44,910 --> 00:02:46,040
I must see him condemned.

49
00:03:04,460 --> 00:03:04,900
Sir.

50
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:07,150
Chang'an and Ruoming are in.

51
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:08,450
Good.

52
00:03:08,810 --> 00:03:10,120
Since he's destroyed

53
00:03:10,130 --> 00:03:11,150
all the evidence outside,

54
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:13,340
we'll go straight into the mine
and find evidence there.

55
00:03:13,750 --> 00:03:15,590
We take Chen Daohua tonight,

56
00:03:15,890 --> 00:03:16,630
dead or alive.

57
00:03:16,940 --> 00:03:17,330
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

58
00:03:19,320 --> 00:03:20,310
I'll leave someone here to protect you.

59
00:03:20,460 --> 00:03:21,360
Don't wander off.

60
00:03:21,360 --> 00:03:21,690
Yes.

61
00:03:22,650 --> 00:03:23,220
Madam Xu,

62
00:03:23,870 --> 00:03:25,690
your safety is tied to Lord Pei's life.

63
00:03:26,190 --> 00:03:26,580
Remember,

64
00:03:27,420 --> 00:03:28,640
you must keep yourself safe.

65
00:03:29,310 --> 00:03:30,520
Don't worry, Lu.

66
00:03:30,520 --> 00:03:31,790
I won't get in the way.

67
00:03:33,710 --> 00:03:34,080
Let's go.

68
00:03:42,610 --> 00:03:43,560
This is my sword.

69
00:03:43,690 --> 00:03:44,630
It's forged with blood jade

70
00:03:44,780 --> 00:03:45,640
and cuts through iron.

71
00:03:45,840 --> 00:03:46,710
Take it for protection.

72
00:03:47,250 --> 00:03:47,850
I have a sword.

73
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:51,150
Go hide.

74
00:03:51,150 --> 00:03:51,750
Yes.

75
00:03:57,860 --> 00:03:58,430
Bad news.

76
00:04:00,060 --> 00:04:01,190
General Chen, bad news.

77
00:04:01,190 --> 00:04:01,750
What is it?

78
00:04:02,310 --> 00:04:03,120
There's a fire outside.

79
00:04:03,520 --> 00:04:04,070
What?

80
00:04:04,670 --> 00:04:05,490
Fire.

81
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:07,640
Put out the fire.

82
00:04:07,760 --> 00:04:08,530
Where's the fire?

83
00:04:09,450 --> 00:04:10,520
- Outside.
- I...

84
00:04:16,050 --> 00:04:16,950
Quick. Put it out.

85
00:04:17,950 --> 00:04:18,730
General Chen,

86
00:04:19,190 --> 00:04:20,160
could these be

87
00:04:20,270 --> 00:04:21,620
next month's tribute?

88
00:04:23,510 --> 00:04:24,080
Darn it.

89
00:04:26,120 --> 00:04:26,630
Wait.

90
00:04:26,630 --> 00:04:27,880
General, where are you going?

91
00:04:48,310 --> 00:04:48,950
Lord Pei.

92
00:04:49,210 --> 00:04:50,400
How dare you trespass into the mine?

93
00:05:05,160 --> 00:05:05,890
Pei Zhao?

94
00:05:06,460 --> 00:05:07,700
Why is he here?

95
00:05:20,190 --> 00:05:20,720
What?

96
00:05:25,160 --> 00:05:27,190
My lord, something seems wrong.

97
00:05:40,180 --> 00:05:45,540
[Garrison Camp]

98
00:05:48,920 --> 00:05:49,350
Don't move.

99
00:05:57,680 --> 00:05:58,800
They fear this flower.

100
00:05:59,480 --> 00:06:00,600
Move carefully.

101
00:06:00,750 --> 00:06:01,720
Don't disturb them.

102
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:02,560
Yes.

103
00:06:07,450 --> 00:06:08,430
What are these?

104
00:06:08,950 --> 00:06:09,310
Gu worms.

105
00:06:10,340 --> 00:06:11,300
Watch out for these worms.

106
00:06:11,460 --> 00:06:12,600
If one gets inside you,

107
00:06:12,600 --> 00:06:13,190
you'll be in real trouble.

108
00:06:15,510 --> 00:06:16,600
Find that Gu worm.

109
00:06:21,430 --> 00:06:22,240
Here it is.

110
00:06:22,670 --> 00:06:23,360
It's not moving.

111
00:06:32,800 --> 00:06:34,310
I wonder if this

112
00:06:34,530 --> 00:06:36,370
can help remove the mother-child Gu.

113
00:06:39,300 --> 00:06:40,470
General Chen is missing.

114
00:06:41,040 --> 00:06:42,120
We don't know if he's alive.

115
00:06:42,960 --> 00:06:44,160
Without my lord's command,

116
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:46,600
no one leaves the camp.

117
00:06:53,930 --> 00:06:55,040
General Chen is here.

118
00:06:57,390 --> 00:06:58,720
Pei Zhao, you scoundrel.

119
00:06:59,240 --> 00:07:01,040
How dare you raid the camp at night?

120
00:07:08,600 --> 00:07:10,390
Kill everyone

121
00:07:10,390 --> 00:07:11,310
who broke into the camp.

122
00:07:15,740 --> 00:07:17,120
You idiot.

123
00:07:17,420 --> 00:07:19,120
Why didn't you call for backup?

124
00:07:30,430 --> 00:07:31,070
Pei Zhao.

125
00:07:31,250 --> 00:07:32,660
I serve the Noble Consort.

126
00:07:32,900 --> 00:07:34,070
How dare you touch me?

127
00:07:34,270 --> 00:07:35,720
Slandering the Noble Consort

128
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:36,670
only adds to your crimes.

129
00:07:42,270 --> 00:07:42,750
Sir.

130
00:07:45,970 --> 00:07:46,350
Sir.

131
00:07:46,540 --> 00:07:47,830
There is a secret tunnel inside.

132
00:07:47,830 --> 00:07:49,670
And there's a lot of blood jade
hidden there.

133
00:08:09,390 --> 00:08:09,750
Sir,

134
00:08:10,270 --> 00:08:11,510
we found many hidden compartments

135
00:08:11,620 --> 00:08:12,530
full of human skeletons.

136
00:08:13,200 --> 00:08:13,950
Skeletons?

137
00:08:14,870 --> 00:08:16,020
Over a hundred.

138
00:08:17,240 --> 00:08:18,310
They were buried in the soil.

139
00:08:18,650 --> 00:08:19,360
Fused with the earth.

140
00:08:20,160 --> 00:08:21,040
It looks like

141
00:08:21,100 --> 00:08:22,160
they've been there for years.

142
00:08:29,950 --> 00:08:32,030
Any sign of who they were?

143
00:08:36,860 --> 00:08:37,240
Sir,

144
00:08:38,240 --> 00:08:39,150
I found this.

145
00:08:41,840 --> 00:08:42,530
Clean everything carefully.

146
00:08:43,140 --> 00:08:44,120
Don't miss a single clue.

147
00:08:44,200 --> 00:08:44,720
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

148
00:08:52,750 --> 00:08:53,870
Everyone, stop.

149
00:08:53,870 --> 00:08:55,220
They don't attack the still.

150
00:08:55,550 --> 00:08:56,960
Stop. Don't move.

151
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:15,410
Sir.

152
00:09:42,360 --> 00:09:43,200
He's dead.

153
00:09:44,370 --> 00:09:46,140
- Mom.
- I want my mom.

154
00:09:46,440 --> 00:09:49,000
Mom.

155
00:09:49,970 --> 00:09:53,390
I want my mom.

156
00:09:53,390 --> 00:09:55,030
Mom.

157
00:09:55,030 --> 00:09:55,960
They are the Wingless.

158
00:09:56,590 --> 00:09:57,210
Yes.

159
00:09:57,630 --> 00:09:58,440
What about the children?

160
00:09:58,580 --> 00:09:59,200
Are they too?

161
00:10:00,200 --> 00:10:00,840
Yes.

162
00:10:01,010 --> 00:10:01,790
Their parents were.

163
00:10:01,790 --> 00:10:02,610
Their children will be.

164
00:10:02,610 --> 00:10:03,720
Generation after generation.

165
00:10:03,920 --> 00:10:04,670
They're born into slavery.

166
00:10:04,920 --> 00:10:05,750
That's their fate.

167
00:10:05,750 --> 00:10:06,840
Didn't you say

168
00:10:06,840 --> 00:10:08,550
the Tianxuan villagers are Wingless too?

169
00:10:08,980 --> 00:10:10,630
Why may they live in a village,

170
00:10:10,870 --> 00:10:12,560
while these people are chained?

171
00:10:12,560 --> 00:10:13,200
[Garrison Camp]

172
00:10:13,200 --> 00:10:15,270
The Wingless never choose their fate.

173
00:10:27,970 --> 00:10:29,200
Do you know

174
00:10:29,470 --> 00:10:31,090
how many petitions

175
00:10:31,300 --> 00:10:32,720
were filed against you today?

176
00:10:34,330 --> 00:10:35,040
Your Majesty,

177
00:10:35,420 --> 00:10:36,550
we were conducting a routine patrol.

178
00:10:36,830 --> 00:10:37,910
When we reached the Blood Jade Mine,

179
00:10:38,020 --> 00:10:39,280
we found a fire inside.

180
00:10:39,600 --> 00:10:40,320
So I led my men in

181
00:10:40,460 --> 00:10:41,090
to put it out.

182
00:10:46,320 --> 00:10:48,130
Quite a story.

183
00:10:50,240 --> 00:10:50,920
Tell me.

184
00:10:51,870 --> 00:10:53,140
What did you find?

185
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:55,170
The tremor last month

186
00:10:55,710 --> 00:10:56,840
wasn't caused by the rebels.

187
00:10:57,160 --> 00:10:58,670
Chen Daohua dug a secret tunnel

188
00:10:58,850 --> 00:10:59,550
to smuggle blood jade.

189
00:11:00,600 --> 00:11:02,670
Chen's theft

190
00:11:02,670 --> 00:11:04,870
and the Crown Prince's ritual,

191
00:11:05,320 --> 00:11:06,470
are these two matters

192
00:11:06,960 --> 00:11:07,990
truly unrelated?

193
00:11:08,630 --> 00:11:09,880
Based on the evidence we have,

194
00:11:10,200 --> 00:11:11,020
there's no connection.

195
00:11:11,600 --> 00:11:12,550
But I believe

196
00:11:12,550 --> 00:11:13,960
there's more to this.

197
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:19,910
Keep investigating.

198
00:11:21,440 --> 00:11:22,120
Yes.

199
00:11:22,750 --> 00:11:24,280
Sir, why hide the truth?

200
00:11:24,670 --> 00:11:26,480
There are too many questions about Chen.

201
00:11:27,140 --> 00:11:28,350
Who was raising the Gu?

202
00:11:28,670 --> 00:11:30,250
Who had him steal the blood jade?

203
00:11:31,120 --> 00:11:32,740
Where was the stolen blood jade taken?

204
00:11:33,960 --> 00:11:35,620
Is the Crown Prince involved?

205
00:11:36,720 --> 00:11:37,720
We have no answers yet.

206
00:11:39,490 --> 00:11:41,050
His Majesty values stability at court.

207
00:11:41,480 --> 00:11:42,410
If we reveal everything now,

208
00:11:42,790 --> 00:11:43,940
we won't be able to keep investigating.

209
00:11:46,950 --> 00:11:47,790
- Your Highness.
- Your Highness.

210
00:11:49,200 --> 00:11:51,150
You're quite capable, Lord Pei.

211
00:11:51,150 --> 00:11:52,440
In just a few days,

212
00:11:52,440 --> 00:11:54,330
you solved the case of the tremor.

213
00:11:55,870 --> 00:11:56,620
I was only doing my duty.

214
00:12:00,090 --> 00:12:01,070
I hear

215
00:12:02,200 --> 00:12:03,600
you've fallen for someone.

216
00:12:04,480 --> 00:12:05,120
Farewell, Your Highness.

217
00:12:07,750 --> 00:12:08,920
Look at you.

218
00:12:09,790 --> 00:12:11,030
I ask you a question,

219
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:12,320
yet you send me away.

220
00:12:13,510 --> 00:12:14,720
But that's

221
00:12:14,720 --> 00:12:16,390
what I like about you.

222
00:12:18,320 --> 00:12:19,480
Let's go.

223
00:12:19,480 --> 00:12:21,120
Don't get in Lord Pei's way.

224
00:12:22,080 --> 00:12:23,240
He's busy.

225
00:12:40,390 --> 00:12:42,150
The Noble Consort has no children.

226
00:12:42,150 --> 00:12:43,150
By rights,

227
00:12:43,600 --> 00:12:45,060
she should protect the Crown Prince.

228
00:12:47,130 --> 00:12:48,030
Could she be

229
00:12:48,030 --> 00:12:49,170
the one behind all this?

230
00:12:52,390 --> 00:12:54,450
But why did she touch your face?

231
00:12:56,070 --> 00:12:57,730
Has she taken a liking to you?

232
00:12:58,750 --> 00:12:59,660
Say it louder.

233
00:12:59,990 --> 00:13:01,180
Let the whole palace hear you.

234
00:13:14,630 --> 00:13:16,160
Master, since you were already there,

235
00:13:16,550 --> 00:13:18,030
why didn't you save General Chen?

236
00:13:24,870 --> 00:13:26,000
The Noble Consort

237
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:27,480
didn't want Pei Zhao harmed.

238
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:29,840
So I gave her what she wanted.

239
00:13:34,390 --> 00:13:36,080
I let Chen Daohua die.

240
00:13:37,030 --> 00:13:38,030
Now,

241
00:13:38,170 --> 00:13:39,550
she should be pleased.

242
00:13:39,740 --> 00:13:41,510
What about the new commander
of the mine?

243
00:13:43,200 --> 00:13:44,240
About that,

244
00:13:47,790 --> 00:13:49,750
I have my own arrangements.

245
00:14:06,100 --> 00:14:06,910
My lady.

246
00:14:09,080 --> 00:14:10,050
How dare you?

247
00:14:10,720 --> 00:14:11,960
How many times have I told you?

248
00:14:11,960 --> 00:14:13,910
No one may disturb me as I play.

249
00:14:13,910 --> 00:14:15,000
Please forgive me, my lady.

250
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:16,820
This is tribute tea
from the Noble Consort.

251
00:14:19,080 --> 00:14:20,030
Leave it.

252
00:14:20,150 --> 00:14:21,000
I'll drink it later.

253
00:14:21,480 --> 00:14:23,730
Your brother has been promoted
to Commander of the Garrison.

254
00:14:24,820 --> 00:14:25,330
Leave.

255
00:14:26,550 --> 00:14:28,270
Why bother practicing the zither?

256
00:14:30,120 --> 00:14:31,630
Even if you cannot play,

257
00:14:31,630 --> 00:14:34,050
you are still the Yun family's jewel.

258
00:14:35,340 --> 00:14:36,190
No.

259
00:14:36,720 --> 00:14:38,520
I must master it.

260
00:14:39,240 --> 00:14:40,150
Back then,

261
00:14:40,150 --> 00:14:42,630
Aunt awed the realm with one song

262
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:44,720
and became the Noble Consort.

263
00:14:45,080 --> 00:14:47,150
If she can make the Yun family proud,

264
00:14:47,440 --> 00:14:47,960
so can I.

265
00:14:48,110 --> 00:14:49,150
That's the spirit.

266
00:14:49,270 --> 00:14:50,850
You don't think I can do it?

267
00:14:52,360 --> 00:14:54,660
In family, beauty, or talent,

268
00:14:55,150 --> 00:14:56,960
few women in Yong

269
00:14:56,960 --> 00:14:58,270
can compare to me.

270
00:14:58,750 --> 00:15:00,240
Even as empress,

271
00:15:00,840 --> 00:15:01,720
I would be worthy.

272
00:15:01,720 --> 00:15:02,870
Of course.

273
00:15:03,320 --> 00:15:05,150
Congratulations on your promotion.

274
00:15:05,270 --> 00:15:06,550
I still need to practice.

275
00:15:06,940 --> 00:15:08,910
This brat made me

276
00:15:08,910 --> 00:15:10,390
[Young Yun Heng]
lose face in front of the guests.

277
00:15:10,570 --> 00:15:12,670
Think about what you've done.

278
00:15:15,910 --> 00:15:16,690
Shao,

279
00:15:17,250 --> 00:15:19,090
look what I bought you.

280
00:15:19,750 --> 00:15:21,810
Mother, I want some too.

281
00:15:22,270 --> 00:15:23,270
[Young Yun Shao]
Your favorite candied hawthorn skewer.

282
00:15:23,270 --> 00:15:24,320
Mother, I want some too.

283
00:15:24,320 --> 00:15:25,080
Mother.

284
00:15:44,570 --> 00:15:45,700
Someone like Yun Qi

285
00:15:46,080 --> 00:15:47,670
gets to command the garrison?

286
00:15:47,670 --> 00:15:49,120
Ruoming, you'd be better than him.

287
00:15:49,120 --> 00:15:50,790
Don't compare me to that scum.

288
00:15:50,900 --> 00:15:51,580
I don't want the job.

289
